uality\n- **Tools**: Snowpipe, Streams, Tasks, Dynamic Tables, Snowpark, dbt, Snowflake CLI\n- **Skills**: SQL proficiency, Python/Java/Scala (Snowpark), ETL/ELT frameworks, data modeling, performance tuning\n\n### Data Analysts\n- **Responsibilities**: Write analytical SQL queries; create secure views; build and consume BI dashboards; validate business metrics; collaborate with product and business teams\n- **Tools**: Snowsight (web UI), BI tools (Power BI, Tableau, Looker), SQL\n- **Skills**: Advanced SQL (window functions, CTEs, aggregates), data interpretation, business acumen\n\n### Snowflake Developers\n- **Responsibilities**: Design and implement data warehouse solutions; write and optimize SQL queries and stored procedures; manage data migrations; configure virtual warehouses, data sharing, and zero-copy cloning; implement security measures (encryption, RBAC, data masking); create and manage data pipelines\n- **Skills**: SQL, data modeling, Snowpark, dbt, performance tuning, security implementation, CI/CD\n\n### Additional Roles\n- **BI Developers**: Create reports, dashboards, and visualizations\n- **Data Scientists**: Explore datasets, run feature engineering, use Snowpark for Python, access training data\n- **DevOps / Cloud Engineers**: Monitor warehouse usage, automate deployments, manage cost controls, set up integrations\n- **Security & Governance Teams**: Implement RBAC, encryption, access controls, masking policies, row access policies, network policies\n- **Database Administrators (DBAs)**: Manage Snowflake environment health, performance, security, backup policies\n\n---\n\n## Snowflake SQL Best Practices\n\n### Naming & Style\n1. **Use snake_case** for all identifiers (tables, columns, CTEs, views). Avoid double-quoted identifiers \u2014 they create case-sensitive names requiring constant quoting.\n2. **Use UPPERCASE for SQL keywords** and **lowercase/snake_case for object names**:\n   ```sql\n   SELECT user_id, event_type FROM prod_db.analytics.e