les:\n  - Full masking: non-privileged roles see `***-**-****` for SSN\n  - Partial masking: show last 4 digits of phone: `***-***-1234`\n- **Tag-based masking**: Apply masking policies to classification tags (e.g., `PII:EMAIL`) so any column with that tag automatically inherits the policy\n- **External tokenization**: Data is tokenized before loading; Snowflake calls an external function to detokenize for authorized users\n\n### 4. Network Security\n- **Network policies** restrict which IP addresses can connect\n- Use **network rules** (modern approach) instead of `ALLOWED_IP_LIST`/`BLOCKED_IP_LIST`:\n  ```sql\n  CREATE NETWORK RULE governance.office_ips TYPE = IPV4 MODE = INGRESS VALUE_LIST = ('203.0.113.0/24');\n  CREATE NETWORK POLICY office_only ALLOWED_NETWORK_RULE_LIST = ('governance.office_ips');\n  ALTER ACCOUNT SET NETWORK_POLICY = office_only;\n  ```\n- Apply policies at account, user, or security integration level\n- Use **AWS PrivateLink** or **Azure PrivateLink** for private connectivity\n- Enable **malicious IP protection** (built-in, default on for new accounts)\n\n### 5. Authentication\n- Enforce **Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)** for all human users (required since Snowflake's 2026 MFA rollout)\n- Use **key-pair authentication** for service accounts (`TYPE = SERVICE` users)\n- Integrate with **SSO** through your identity provider (Okta, Azure AD, etc.)\n- Use **SCIM** for automated user lifecycle management\n\n### 6. Auditing & Monitoring\n- Use **`ACCESS_HISTORY`** view (in `ACCOUNT_USAGE` schema) to track which columns were accessed by which queries \u2014 retains data for 365 days\n- Use **`QUERY_HISTORY`** for complete query audit trail\n- Use **`POLICY_REFERENCES`** to audit where masking and row access policies are applied\n- Set up **weekly reports** for PII access auditing\n- Export `ACCESS_HISTORY` to a separate table for longer retention\n\n### 7. Data Classification\n- Use **object tagging** to classify data (PII, PHI, FINANCIAL, INTERNAL, PUBLIC)\n- Enable **automatic sensitive data classification** via classification profiles (`ALTER DATABASE ... SET CLASSIFICATION_PROFILE`)\n- Use **`SYSTEM$CLASSIFY`** to test classification on individual tables\n- Apply governance policies via tags \u2014 classify once, enforce everywhere\n\n### 8. Secure Views\n- Use **secure views** for anything involving sensitive data or row filtering logic\n- Secure views **hide the view definition** and **prevent the optimizer from pushing user predicates** into the view query\n- Tradeoff: secure views can be **10\u201320% slower** than regular views\n- Use regular views for everything else\n\n### 9. Environment Isolation\n- Use **separate accounts** for production vs. non-production environments\n- Apply different network policies per environment (tighter for production)\n- Use **data sharing** for cross-environment access without copying data\n\n### 10. Data Encryption\n- Snowflake automatically encrypts data **at rest** and **in transit**\n- Use **Tri-Secret Secure (TSS)** encryption for enhanced protection\n- Manage encryption keys via **customer-managed keys** (CMK) through your cloud provider's KMS\n\n---\n\n## Naming Conventions Summary\n\n| Object Type | Naming Convention | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Database** | `[ENV]_[PROJECT/PROGRAM]_[DATA_LAYER]_DB` | `PROD_FINANCE_STAGING_DB` |\n| **Schema** | `[DATA_GROUPING]` (by source or normalization technique) | `RAW.HUBSPOT`, `DW.DIM` |\n| **Table** | `[TABLE_NAME]` (singular, snake_case) | `customer_orders` |\n| **View** | `[VIEW_NAME]` or `vw_[name]` | `customer_summary` or `vw_customer` |\n| **Warehouse** | `[ENV]_[PROJECT/PROGRAM]_[ROLE_NAME]_[WH_SIZE]` | `PROD_ANALYTICS_ANALYST_WH_L` |\n| **Role** | `[ENV]_[ROLE_NAME]` | `PROD_DATA_ENGINEER` |\n| **Stage** | `[NAME]_[TYPE]_STG` | `S3_STG` |\n| **Snowpipe** | `[NAME]_PIPE` | `orders_pipe` |\n| **Stream** | `[NAME]_STREAM` | `orders_stream` |\n| **Task** | `[NAME]_TASK` | `orders_task` |\n| **Stored Procedure